WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.912
Checkpoint question. Your agent retrieves useful chunks, but it rewrites the query on every run until the step limit.

00:00:08.912 --> 00:00:11.352
What should you inspect first?

00:00:11.352 --> 00:00:14.127
Not the size of the vector database.

00:00:14.127 --> 00:00:18.486
Not model temperature. Inspect the grader and its threshold.

00:00:19.444 --> 00:00:26.736
If the grader never allows the generate route, the workflow will keep correcting even when evidence is already useful.

00:00:26.736 --> 00:00:32.911
The correct answer is: inspect the grader and its threshold before changing the architecture.
